2025-05-01 02:26:39 - Thread-863 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Relevant tables / columns for finding TCGA‑LAML cases with the largest weighted‑average copy number in cytoband 15q11  
(“weight” = segment_mean × num_probes ; “average” = Σ weight / Σ num_probes within the cytoband).

1. TCGA_MITELMAN.TCGA_VERSIONED.COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED_HG38_GDC_2017_02  
   • "project_short_name" – pick the study (“TCGA‑LAML”).  
   • "case_barcode" – final identifier we need.  
   • "sample_barcode", "aliquot_barcode" – optional sample‑level details.  
   • "chromosome" – filter to 15.  
   • "start_pos", "end_pos" – genomic coordinates for overlap.  
   • "segment_mean" – log2 copy‑number value.  
   • "num_probes" – probe count (weight).

2. TCGA_MITELMAN.PROD.CYTOBANDS_HG38  
   • "chromosome" – e.g. ‘chr15’.  
   • "hg38_start", "hg38_stop" – coordinate range of each cytoband.  
   • "cytoband_name" – pick ‘15q11’.

Typical conditions  
• cns."project_short_name" = 'TCGA-LAML'  
• cns."chromosome" = '15'  
• cb."chromosome" = 'chr15' AND cb."cytoband_name" = '15q11'  
• overlap test: cns."end_pos" >= cb."hg38_start" AND cns."start_pos" <= cb."hg38_stop'

------------------------------------------------------------------
Example Snowflake SQL queries (10, from exploratory to final).  
(Replace DATABASE/SCHEMA/TABLE with the exact names shown; all columns are double‑quoted).

```sql
-- 1. Description: Show the coordinate range for cytoband 15q11 on chr15.
SELECT *
FROM "TCGA_MITELMAN"."PROD"."CYTOBANDS_HG38"
WHERE "chromosome" = 'chr15'
  AND "cytoband_name" = '15q11'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: List all studies present in the HG38 masked segment table.
SELECT DISTINCT "project_short_name"
FROM "TCGA_MITELMAN"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED_HG38_GDC_2017_02"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Preview a few LAML segments on chromosome 15.
SELECT *
FROM "TCGA_MITELMAN"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED_HG38_GDC_2017_02" c
WHERE c."project_short_name" = 'TCGA-LAML'
  AND c."chromosome" = '15'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Join segments with the 15q11 cytoband to keep only overlapping rows.
SELECT c."case_barcode",
       c."start_pos",
       c."end_pos",
       c."segment_mean",
       c."num_probes"
FROM "TCGA_MITELMAN"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED_HG38_GDC_2017_02"  c
JOIN "TCGA_MITELMAN"."PROD"."CYTOBANDS_HG38" cb
     ON cb."chromosome" = 'chr15'
    AND cb."cytoband_name" = '15q11'
    AND c."chromosome" = '15'
    AND c."end_pos"   >= cb."hg38_start"
    AND c."start_pos" <= cb."hg38_stop"
WHERE c."project_short_name" = 'TCGA-LAML'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Compute per‑segment weight contribution inside 15q11.
SELECT c."case_barcode",
       (c."segment_mean" * c."num_probes")        AS "weighted_value",
       c."num_probes"
FROM "TCGA_MITELMAN"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED_HG38_GDC_2017_02"  c
JOIN "TCGA_MITELMAN"."PROD"."CYTOBANDS_HG38" cb
     ON cb."chromosome" = 'chr15'
    AND cb."cytoband_name" = '15q11'
    AND c."chromosome" = '15'
    AND c."end_pos"   >= cb."hg38_start"
    AND c."start_pos" <= cb."hg38_stop"
WHERE c."project_short_name" = 'TCGA-LAML'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Aggregate to get Σ weight and Σ probes per case.
SELECT c."case_barcode",
       SUM(c."segment_mean" * c."num_probes") AS "sum_weight",
       SUM(c."num_probes")                    AS "sum_probes"
FROM "TCGA_MITELMAN"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED_HG38_GDC_2017_02"  c
JOIN "TCGA_MITELMAN"."PROD"."CYTOBANDS_HG38" cb
     ON cb."chromosome" = 'chr15'
    AND cb."cytoband_name" = '15q11'
    AND c."chromosome" = '15'
    AND c."end_pos"   >= cb."hg38_start"
    AND c."start_pos" <= cb."hg38_stop"
WHERE c."project_short_name" = 'TCGA-LAML'
GROUP BY c."case_barcode"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Calculate the weighted average copy number per case.
SELECT c."case_barcode",
       SUM(c."segment_mean" * c."num_probes") / NULLIF(SUM(c."num_probes"),0) AS "weighted_avg_cn"
FROM "TCGA_MITELMAN"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED_HG38_GDC_2017_02"  c
JOIN "TCGA_MITELMAN"."PROD"."CYTOBANDS_HG38" cb
     ON cb."chromosome" = 'chr15'
    AND cb."cytoband_name" = '15q11'
    AND c."chromosome" = '15'
    AND c."end_pos"   >= cb."hg38_start"
    AND c."start_pos" <= cb."hg38_stop"
WHERE c."project_short_name" = 'TCGA-LAML'
GROUP BY c."case_barcode"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Same as #7 but ordered to show the highest averages first.
SELECT c."case_barcode",
       SUM(c."segment_mean" * c."num_probes") / NULLIF(SUM(c."num_probes"),0) AS "weighted_avg_cn"
FROM "TCGA_MITELMAN"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED_HG38_GDC_2017_02"  c
JOIN "TCGA_MITELMAN"."PROD"."CYTOBANDS_HG38" cb
     ON cb."chromosome" = 'chr15'
    AND cb."cytoband_name" = '15q11'
    AND c."chromosome" = '15'
    AND c."end_pos"   >= cb."hg38_start"
    AND c."start_pos" <= cb."hg38_stop"
WHERE c."project_short_name" = 'TCGA-LAML'
GROUP BY c."case_barcode"
ORDER BY "weighted_avg_cn" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Drill down to sample‑level averages (optional exploratory step).
SELECT c."case_barcode",
       c."sample_barcode",
       SUM(c."segment_mean" * c."num_probes") / NULLIF(SUM(c."num_probes"),0) AS "weighted_avg_cn"
FROM "TCGA_MITELMAN"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED_HG38_GDC_2017_02"  c
JOIN "TCGA_MITELMAN"."PROD"."CYTOBANDS_HG38" cb
     ON cb."chromosome" = 'chr15'
    AND cb."cytoband_name" = '15q11'
    AND c."chromosome" = '15'
    AND c."end_pos"   >= cb."hg38_start"
    AND c."start_pos" <= cb."hg38_stop"
WHERE c."project_short_name" = 'TCGA-LAML'
GROUP BY c."case_barcode", c."sample_barcode"
ORDER BY "weighted_avg_cn" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: FINAL – return the TCGA‑LAML case(s) with the single highest weighted‑average
-- copy number in cytoband 15q11 (ties included).
WITH band AS (
    SELECT "hg38_start" AS "b_start", "hg38_stop" AS "b_stop"
    FROM   "TCGA_MITELMAN"."PROD"."CYTOBANDS_HG38"
    WHERE  "chromosome" = 'chr15'
      AND  "cytoband_name" = '15q11'
),
calc AS (
    SELECT c."case_barcode",
           SUM(c."segment_mean" * c."num_probes") / NULLIF(SUM(c."num_probes"),0) AS "weighted_avg_cn"
    FROM "TCGA_MITELMAN"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED_HG38_GDC_2017_02"  c,
         band b
    WHERE c."project_short_name" = 'TCGA-LAML'
      AND c."chromosome" = '15'
      AND c."end_pos"   >= b."b_start"
      AND c."start_pos" <= b."b_stop"
    GROUP BY c."case_barcode"
),
maxval AS (
    SELECT MAX("weighted_avg_cn") AS "top_cn" FROM calc
)
SELECT calc."case_barcode", calc."weighted_avg_cn"
FROM   calc
JOIN   maxval ON calc."weighted_avg_cn" = maxval."top_cn"
LIMIT 20;
```

These queries provide a step‑by‑step pathway—from inspecting required coordinates to computing and returning the TCGA‑LAML case barcodes with the highest weighted average copy number in cytoband 15q11.
